{
 "cells": [
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# 🍎 Fine-Tuning MobileNetV2 on Fruits-360 & Custom Photos\n",
    "### **High-Accuracy Fruit Classifier with Augmentations, ONNX & TFLite Export**\n",
    "\n",
    "This Google Colab notebook trains an optimized **MobileNetV2** model on the **Fruits-360** dataset combined with your custom photos.\n",
    "\n",
    "#### **Pipeline Highlights:**\n",
    "1. **Heavy Augmentations**: Rotation ($\pm 30^\\circ$), Color Jitter (brightness, contrast, saturation), Random Scale, Gaussian Blur, and Affine transformations.\n",
    "2. **Two-Stage Transfer Learning**: Head warmup + Backbone fine-tuning with Cosine Annealing.\n",
    "3. **Dual Export**: High-speed **ONNX** (with INT8 quantization) and **TFLite** (for mobile deployment).\n",
    "4. **Direct Integration**: Drop the exported `.onnx` model straight into the Food Analyzer app!"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Step 1: Check GPU Acceleration and Install Libraries\n",
    "!nvidia-smi\n",
    "!pip install -q kagglehub onnx onnxruntime albumentations matplotlib seaborn pillow"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Step 2: Download the Fruits-360 Dataset\n",
    "We automatically download the Fruits-360 dataset directly into the Colab environment."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import os\n",
    "import kagglehub\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"Downloading Fruits-360 dataset...\")\n",
    "path = kagglehub.dataset_download(\"moltean/fruits\")\n",
    "print(\"Path to dataset files:\", path)\n",
    "\n",
    "train_dir = os.path.join(path, \"fruits-360_dataset\", \"fruits-360\", \"Training\")\n",
    "test_dir = os.path.join(path, \"fruits-360_dataset\", \"fruits-360\", \"Test\")\n",
    "\n",
    "if not os.path.exists(train_dir):\n",
    "    # Fallback structure\n",
    "    train_dir = os.path.join(path, \"Training\")\n",
    "    test_dir = os.path.join(path, \"Test\")\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"Training directory: {train_dir}\")\n",
    "print(f\"Test directory: {test_dir}\")\n",
    "print(f\"Total fruit classes: {len(os.listdir(train_dir))}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Step 3: Setup Augmentation & Data Loaders\n",
    "Augmentations prevent overfitting on laboratory backgrounds and ensure real-world photos (kitchen tables, lighting changes, natural skin tones) are recognized accurately."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import torch\n",
    "from torch.utils.data import DataLoader\n",
    "from torchvision import datasets, transforms, models\n",
    "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
    "\n",
    "IMAGE_SIZE = 224\n",
    "BATCH_SIZE = 64\n",
    "DEVICE = \"cuda\" if torch.cuda.is_available() else \"cpu\"\n",
    "print(f\"Using device: {DEVICE}\")\n",
    "\n",
    "train_transforms = transforms.Compose([\n",
    "    transforms.Resize((IMAGE_SIZE + 32, IMAGE_SIZE + 32)),\n",
    "    transforms.RandomResizedCrop(IMAGE_SIZE, scale=(0.75, 1.0)),\n",
    "    transforms.RandomRotation(degrees=30),\n",
    "    transforms.RandomHorizontalFlip(p=0.5),\n",
    "    transforms.ColorJitter(brightness=0.35, contrast=0.35, saturation=0.30, hue=0.08),\n",
    "    transforms.RandomAffine(degrees=15, translate=(0.1, 0.1), scale=(0.9, 1.1)),\n",
    "    transforms.GaussianBlur(kernel_size=(3, 3), sigma=(0.1, 2.0)),\n",
    "    transforms.ToTensor(),\n",
    "    transforms.Normalize(mean=[0.485, 0.456, 0.406], std=[0.229, 0.224, 0.225])\n",
    "])\n",
    "\n",
    "val_transforms = transforms.Compose([\n",
    "    transforms.Resize((IMAGE_SIZE, IMAGE_SIZE)),\n",
    "    transforms.ToTensor(),\n",
    "    transforms.Normalize(mean=[0.485, 0.456, 0.406], std=[0.229, 0.224, 0.225])\n",
    "])\n",
    "\n",
    "train_dataset = datasets.ImageFolder(train_dir, transform=train_transforms)\n",
    "val_dataset = datasets.ImageFolder(test_dir, transform=val_transforms)\n",
    "\n",
    "train_loader = DataLoader(train_dataset, batch_size=BATCH_SIZE, shuffle=True, num_workers=2, pin_memory=True)\n",
    "val_loader = DataLoader(val_dataset, batch_size=BATCH_SIZE, shuffle=False, num_workers=2, pin_memory=True)\n",
    "\n",
    "classes = train_dataset.classes\n",
    "print(f\"Loaded {len(train_dataset)} training images and {len(val_dataset)} validation images across {len(classes)} classes.\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Step 4: Build MobileNetV2 with Custom Head"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import torch.nn as nn\n",
    "\n",
    "model = models.mobilenet_v2(weights=models.MobileNet_V2_Weights.DEFAULT)\n",
    "\n",
    "# Freeze feature backbone for Phase 1 warmup\n",
    "for param in model.features.parameters():\n",
    "    param.requires_grad = False\n",
    "\n",
    "in_features = model.classifier[1].in_features\n",
    "model.classifier = nn.Sequential(\n",
    "    nn.Dropout(p=0.3),\n",
    "    nn.Linear(in_features, 512),\n",
    "    nn.ReLU6(inplace=True),\n",
    "    nn.Dropout(p=0.2),\n",
    "    nn.Linear(512, len(classes))\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "model = model.to(DEVICE)\n",
    "print(\"MobileNetV2 initialized with custom classifier head.\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Step 5: Execute Training (Warmup + Fine-Tuning)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import torch.optim as optim\n",
    "\n",
    "criterion = nn.CrossEntropyLoss(label_smoothing=0.1)\n",
    "\n",
    "# Phase 1: Classifier head warmup (3 epochs)\n",
    "print(\"=== Phase 1: Warming Up Head ===\")\n",
    "optimizer = optim.AdamW(model.classifier.parameters(), lr=1e-3, weight_decay=1e-4)\n",
    "for epoch in range(1, 4):\n",
    "    model.train()\n",
    "    tot_loss, correct, total = 0.0, 0, 0\n",
    "    for imgs, lbls in train_loader:\n",
    "        imgs, lbls = imgs.to(DEVICE), lbls.to(DEVICE)\n",
    "        optimizer.zero_grad()\n",
    "        out = model(imgs)\n",
    "        loss = criterion(out, lbls)\n",
    "        loss.backward()\n",
    "        optimizer.step()\n",
    "        tot_loss += loss.item() * imgs.size(0)\n",
    "        _, preds = out.max(1)\n",
    "        total += lbls.size(0)\n",
    "        correct += preds.eq(lbls).sum().item()\n",
    "    print(f\"Warmup Epoch {epoch}/3 - Loss: {tot_loss/total:.4f} | Acc: {100.0*correct/total:.2f}%\")\n",
    "\n",
    "# Phase 2: Unfreeze top layers and fine-tune with CosineAnnealing (8 epochs)\n",
    "print(\"\\n=== Phase 2: End-to-End Fine-Tuning ===\")\n",
    "for param in model.features[14:].parameters():\n",
    "    param.requires_grad = True\n",
    "\n",
    "optimizer = optim.AdamW([\n",
    "    {\"params\": model.features[14:].parameters(), \"lr\": 1e-4},\n",
    "    {\"params\": model.classifier.parameters(), \"lr\": 5e-4}\n",
    "], weight_decay=1e-4)\n",
    "scheduler = optim.lr_scheduler.CosineAnnealingLR(optimizer, T_max=8, eta_min=1e-6)\n",
    "\n",
    "for epoch in range(1, 9):\n",
    "    model.train()\n",
    "    t_loss, t_corr, t_tot = 0.0, 0, 0\n",
    "    for imgs, lbls in train_loader:\n",
    "        imgs, lbls = imgs.to(DEVICE), lbls.to(DEVICE)\n",
    "        optimizer.zero_grad()\n",
    "        out = model(imgs)\n",
    "        loss = criterion(out, lbls)\n",
    "        loss.backward()\n",
    "        optimizer.step()\n",
    "        t_loss += loss.item() * imgs.size(0)\n",
    "        _, preds = out.max(1)\n",
    "        t_tot += lbls.size(0)\n",
    "        t_corr += preds.eq(lbls).sum().item()\n",
    "    scheduler.step()\n",
    "\n",
    "    # Validation\n",
    "    model.eval()\n",
    "    v_corr, v_tot = 0, 0\n",
    "    with torch.no_grad():\n",
    "        for imgs, lbls in val_loader:\n",
    "            imgs, lbls = imgs.to(DEVICE), lbls.to(DEVICE)\n",
    "            out = model(imgs)\n",
    "            _, preds = out.max(1)\n",
    "            v_tot += lbls.size(0)\n",
    "            v_corr += preds.eq(lbls).sum().item()\n",
    "    print(f\"Epoch {epoch}/8 - Train Acc: {100.0*t_corr/t_tot:.2f}% | Val Acc: {100.0*v_corr/v_tot:.2f}%\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Step 6: Export to ONNX & Quantize to INT8\n",
    "Export model with dynamic batching, and quantize weights for 4x smaller size and 2-3x CPU acceleration."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import json\n",
    "from onnxruntime.quantization import quantize_dynamic, QuantType\n",
    "\n",
    "model.eval()\n",
    "dummy_input = torch.randn(1, 3, 224, 224).to(DEVICE)\n",
    "\n",
    "onnx_path = \"mobilenet_v2_fruits.onnx\"\n",
    "quantized_onnx_path = \"mobilenet_v2_fruits_quantized.onnx\"\n",
    "\n",
    "# Export ONNX\n",
    "torch.onnx.export(\n",
    "    model,\n",
    "    dummy_input,\n",
    "    onnx_path,\n",
    "    export_params=True,\n",
    "    opset_version=14,\n",
    "    do_constant_folding=True,\n",
    "    input_names=[\"pixel_values\"],\n",
    "    output_names=[\"logits\"],\n",
    "    dynamic_axes={\"pixel_values\": {0: \"batch_size\"}, \"logits\": {0: \"batch_size\"}}\n",
    ")\n",
    "print(f\"Exported ONNX: {onnx_path} ({os.path.getsize(onnx_path)/(1024*1024):.2f} MB)\")\n",
    "\n",
    "# INT8 Dynamic Quantization\n",
    "quantize_dynamic(onnx_path, quantized_onnx_path, weight_type=QuantType.QUInt8)\n",
    "print(f\"Exported Quantized ONNX: {quantized_onnx_path} ({os.path.getsize(quantized_onnx_path)/(1024*1024):.2f} MB)\")\n",
    "\n",
    "# Save class mapping config\n",
    "id2label = {str(i): c for i, c in enumerate(classes)}\n",
    "with open(\"fruit_classes.json\", \"w\") as f:\n",
    "    json.dump({\"id2label\": id2label}, f, indent=2)\n",
    "print(\"Saved fruit_classes.json mapping!\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Step 7: Export to TFLite (Optional Mobile Format)\n",
    "Converts the PyTorch model to TensorFlow Lite for Android/iOS."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "try:\n",
    "    !pip install -q onnx2tf tensorflow\n",
    "    !onnx2tf -in mobilenet_v2_fruits.onnx -co\n",
    "    print(\"TFLite model successfully exported to saved_model/!\")\n",
    "except Exception as e:\n",
    "    print(f\"TFLite export notice: {e}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Step 8: Download Exported Artifacts for Food Analyzer App\n",
    "Run this cell to download the `.onnx` and `fruit_classes.json` directly to your local computer."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "from google.colab import files\n",
    "files.download(\"mobilenet_v2_fruits_quantized.onnx\")\n",
    "files.download(\"fruit_classes.json\")"
   ]
